> | Fuel Adjustment | Variable rate tied to current fuel index | $30 |  
> | Insurance Premium | 1 % of total value of goods (assumed $30,000) | $300 |  
> | Extra Padding (optional) | Premium cushioning for fragile items | $50 |  
> | Expedited Service (optional) | 20 % surcharge for same‑day delivery | $70 |  

**Base Fare**  
The base fare covers the movers’ time, equipment, and the essential labor of lifting, securing, and transporting your belongings. It is a fixed amount that guarantees a minimum charge regardless of the job’s length or complexity. In this example, the base fare is **$350**.

**Distance Surcharge**  
After the first 10 miles, a distance surcharge kicks in at $2.50 per mile. For a 30‑mile trip, the surcharge totals **$75**. This ensures that longer routes, which require more fuel and time, are priced fairly.

**Fuel Adjustment**  
Fuel prices fluctuate, so a fuel adjustment protects both the mover and the customer from sudden spikes. The adjustment is calculated as a percentage of the base fare and the distance surcharge. Here it amounts to **$30**.

**Insurance Premium**  
A 1 % insurance premium on the declared value of your items (assumed $30,000) adds a safety net for loss or damage. The premium in this scenario is **$300**.

**Optional Add‑Ons**  

**Total Cost**  
Adding all mandatory charges gives **$705**. Including both optional add‑ons pushes the total to **$805**. This structured approach makes the moving cost transparent, allowing you to weigh the benefits of add‑ons against their impact on the final bill.</div>
